# Fixture

PROVIDES fixture infrastructure
SO THAT node-status tests
CAN pin results to read paths

## Assertions

### Scenarios

- Given a first input, when it is processed, then the first output is produced ([test](tests/first.scenario.l1.test.ts))
- Given a second input, when it is processed, then the second output is produced ([test](tests/second.scenario.l1.test.ts))

### Compliance

- ALWAYS: the first rule holds ([audit:rule-one])
- NEVER: the second rule is broken ([audit:rule-two])
